"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/14/pbf-energy-inc-pbf-q4-2018-earnings-conference-cal.aspx"},{"c":"PBF 2019 Q1","e":"pbf","d":"2019-05-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Neil Mehta","x":"And then the follow up is just on California, a lot of noise and speculation right now, about constraints in California, crude supply potentially over time with the bill passing through the assembly.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/02/pbf-energy-pbf-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PBF 2019 Q1","e":"pbf","d":"2019-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Erik Young","x":"We felt very firmly that putting in place a long-term balance sheet, essentially restructuring and refinancing our ABL, as well as the acquisition revolver at PBFX in 2018 was the prudent move, which would ultimately allow us enough flexibility to get through quarters like this.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/02/pbf-energy-pbf-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PBF 2020 Q1","e":"pbf","d":"2020-05-15","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tom Nimbley","x":"Our total projected cost-reduction measures amount to more than $600 million in expected savings in 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/16/pbf-energy-pbf-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PBF 2020 Q2","e":"pbf","d":"2020-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Matt Lucey","x":"The company has been effective at streamlining and gaining more efficiency out of our own workforce, which has allowed us to reduce headcount, reduce overtime, and the total number of contractors in our facilities.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/01/pbf-energy-pbf-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"PBF 2020 Q3","e":"pbf","d":"2020-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Matthew Blair","x":"And do you feel that, just the overall looser environment, does that make it tougher to pass-through any RIN cost to the end consumer?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/pbf-energy-pbf-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2020 Q3","e":"pbf","d":"2020-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Erik Young","x":"This is partially offset by roughly $15 million in expected legal and severance costs associated with the reconfiguration.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/pbf-energy-pbf-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2020 Q3","e":"pbf","d":"2020-10-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Erik Young","x":"I don't think we're going to get into that level of detail across the board, but you should start to see the benefits from the cost savings run through in Q1 of 2021 in the East Coast segment of our financials.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/30/pbf-energy-pbf-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2020 Q4","e":"pbf","d":"2021-02-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tom Nimbley","x":"We expect initial results of our ongoing cost reduction programs will generate an incremental $100 million to $125 million in operating expense savings for the rest of our refining system.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/11/pbf-energy-pbf-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2020 Q4","e":"pbf","d":"2021-02-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Erik Young","x":"Included in our results for the quarter was the previously disclosed severance expense included in G&A related to the East Coast refining reconfiguration.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/11/pbf-energy-pbf-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2021 Q1","e":"pbf","d":"2021-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Matt Lucey","x":"It's more of a pass-through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/pbf-energy-pbf-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2021 Q1","e":"pbf","d":"2021-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Tom Nimbley","x":"And one of the things that are being discussed is to go to more of an LCFS program, which, as you all know, I'm sure that is all passed through to the consumer 100%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/pbf-energy-pbf-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2021 Q1","e":"pbf","d":"2021-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Erik Young","x":"So our cost savings were actually a lot more than what we're reporting because our variable costs are down and all that stuff.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/pbf-energy-pbf-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2022 Q2","e":"pbf","d":"2022-07-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Connor Lynagh","x":"Just in terms of the strategic thinking, obviously, you highlighted the cost savings and some of the mechanical savings not having run to super companies, but just strategically thinking -- what's your sort of thought on the value creation there?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/07/29/pbf-energy-pbf-q2-2022-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"PBF 2026 Q3","e":"pbf","d":"2026-10-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Joseph Marino","x":"Higher commodity prices are generally a tailwind to working capital, but as a significant portion of the price increases occurred late in the quarter, we are seeing benefits flow through in early Q4.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/29/pbf-energy-pbf-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[35,1,9682,0,0,0,7598,1573],[36,1,11052,1,1,0,8127,2334],[37,1,9080,0,0,0,6815,1874],[38,1,7923,0,0,0,5919,1670],[39,1,7194,0,0,0,5421,1416],[40,1,7298,0,0,0,5573,1353],[41,1,10829,0,0,0,8472,1929],[42,1,7908,0,0,0,5758,1816],[43,1,7805,0,0,0,5813,1613],[44,1,6747,0,0,0,5612,858],[45,1,7318,0,0,0,5793,1169],[46,1,9714,0,0,0,7542,1751],[47,1,7062,0,0,0,5378,1323],[48,1,9029,0,0,0,6704,